+## D8 — Split bare and spectator zero-header rows (review-7444e31d07487847)
+
+**Observed coverage hole.** Version 2.0 always placed a foreign spectator before
+markers in the generated zero-header row. That correctly defeated
+first-nonzero-key rules, but it never emitted a marker-only zero-header row. The
+conditional rule “borrow the nearest colored header only for marker-only rows”
+therefore fit all canonical and generated support while differing on a lawful
+input. Public scalar arguments also accepted booleans/coercible values through
+Python indexing before validation.
+
+**Repair.** Version 2.1 publishes `LESSON_SCHEDULE_PERIOD = 2`. Core draws contain
+a genuinely bare zero-header marker row whose interior is only 0/8; rich draws
+retain the spectator-before-marker witness. Palette completion is forbidden from
+placing missing colors into the core bare row. The new
+`nearest_key_for_marker_only_rows` rival and `bare_zero_header_marker` witness
+make the missing hypothesis executable. Seed and sample index require exact
+integers, sample index is nonnegative, and difficulty is restricted to
+None/easy/medium/hard before sampling.
+
+**Verification.** The final suite passes 73 tests. Lint, self-check, rule smoke,
+override, rotation-sensitive semantic enumeration, and authority synchronization
+passed. The reusable `workspace/bare_zero_header_audit.py` replayed 18 generated
+cases plus all three canonical pairs in 21 protected-Racket evaluations: exactly
+nine core cases had bare rows, nine rich cases had spectator rows, every declared
+rival was defeated, and the new conditional rival differed on all nine core
+cases while fitting all nine rich cases.
+
+**Limit.** The audit is finite and restricted to declared competitors. The source
+remains an owner-reviewed repair proposal until exact-source acceptance; no
+training admission is implied.
