+## Zero-header branch replay
+
+`bare_zero_header_audit.py` is the compact current-source check for the v2.1
+curriculum split. It verifies core bare rows versus rich spectator rows,
+protected-Racket parity, canonical rival fit, declared-rival defeats, scalar
+rejection, determinism, and exact source hashes.
+
+```bash
+python3 review.py run --receipt checks/0d5077971eea/zero-header-command.json \
+  python3 generators/0d5077971eea/workspace/bare_zero_header_audit.py \
+  --out ../checks/0d5077971eea/zero_header_audit.json
+```
+
+The retained audit uses 18 generated cases and all canonical pairs. It is a
+bounded regression tool rather than a universal identifiability proof.
